 "person": [
  "look at the screen while look 2 plays for each outcome (the tool shows it for about two seconds and removes it): the trophy with turning rays and confetti, the rain cloud and the droopy face, the clasp, the finish flag, the clock with a sweeping hand, the crown over a ribbon with sparkles; say if anything flickers, tears or stutters, and if the buttons read as buttons",
  "the results that matter are in result.json for each look and outcome: entry_us (the full-screen frame when the screen appears; the gate is 100 ms), us_mean and us_worst (the frames after it, one refresh per 30 ms step: the gates are 18,000 us worst at look 0, 15,000 at look 1, and at look 2 (the light motion) 8,000 mean and 25,000 worst), objects (2 at looks 1 and 2, about 12 at look 0), and internal_free_before and internal_free_during per look. The frame times must be the real flush, not the draw calls only (bench_over's timing was asked of the firmware track)."
